WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
First, check the data label
DEMO DATA · SYNTHETIC means the lab is teaching with generated numbers. Its dates and changes are not evidence of an actual flood.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:16.000
Choose Before and After
Choose an earlier and a later frame. The timeline plays stored frames; it does not create observations between dates. T1 to T6 are frame labels.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Set the change threshold
The threshold is the minimum absolute radar difference to mark a candidate. A higher threshold usually selects fewer cells. It is not a confidence percentage.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Understand smoothing
The 3 × 3 option averages nearby valid measurements in linear power, then displays them in dB. It can reduce local variation but also blur small features.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Run, then read the result
Candidate cells crossed the threshold. Mean signed change describes the average direction. Zero candidates can coexist with a nonzero mean when changes are below the threshold.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:48.000
Check what is still unknown
Not available is not zero. Review sources, exclusions and limitations in the receipts. Ask the data explains available evidence using fixed templates; it cannot confirm a flood.
